ENFORCEMENT DECREE OF THE FRAMEWORK ACT ON THE PROMOTION OF THE HALLYU INDUSTRY

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters delegated by the Framework Act on the Promotion of the Hallyu Industry and matters necessary for its enforcement.

Article 2 (Products Related to Hallyu)
The term "products prescribed by Presidential Decree" in subparagraph 3 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on the Promotion of the Hallyu Industry (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following products:
1. Tourism products, such as transportation, accommodation, food, entertainment, recreation, or services, provided for tourists by tourism business operators under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Tourism Promotion Act;
2. Food under subparagraph 7 of Article 3 of the Framework Act on Agriculture, Rural Community and Food Industry;
3. Fishery food under subparagraph 3 of Article 2 of the Act on the Development of and Support for the Fishery Food Industry;
4. Traditional cultural products under subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Traditional Culture Industry Promotion Act;
5. Cosmetics under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Cosmetics Act;
6. Other products related to Hallyu that the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism publicly notifies after consultation with the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies.

Article 3 (Formulation of Medium- and Long-Term Master Plans)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall formulate a medium- and long-term master plan for the promotion of the Hallyu industry and Hallyu-related industries (hereinafter referred to as "Hallyu industries, etc.") under Article 6 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "master plan") by September 30 of the year preceding the year in which each five-year period begins.
(2) When amending the master plan, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall consult with the heads of the relevant administrative agencies: Provided, That this shall not apply when amending any of the following minor matters:
1. An amendment to reflect amendments to the Act or this Decree, or the enactment, amendment, or repeal of other statutes or regulations;
2. Correction of a simple mistake, clerical error, omission, or a comparable manifest error;
3. An amendment to any other matter that does not affect the basic direction of the master plan and for which the grounds for amendment are clear.
(3) When the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism formulates or amends the master plan, the Minister shall publicly announce its contents on the website of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 4 (Formulation of Implementation Plans)
(1) An implementation plan for the promotion of Hallyu industries, etc. under Article 7 (1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as an "implementation plan") shall include the following matters:
1. The direction for carrying out projects in the relevant year and detailed implementation plans for each major project;
2. The results of implementing the previous year's implementation plan;
3. Matters concerning cooperation with the relevant central administrative agencies to promote Hallyu industries, etc.;
4. Other matters necessary to promote Hallyu industries, etc.
(2) After consultation with the heads of the relevant central administrative agencies, the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall formulate the implementation plan for the following year by December 31 each year and notify the heads of those agencies thereof.
(3) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall analyze and evaluate the results of implementing implementation plans and reflect the results in the next master plan and implementation plan, respectively.

Article 5 (Hallyu Policy Council)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may establish a Hallyu Policy Council (hereinafter referred to as the "Council") to consult on and coordinate the following matters for the smooth implementation of policies concerning Hallyu and Hallyu industries, etc.:
1. Matters concerning the formulation of a master plan or implementation plan and related matters;
2. Matters concerning products publicly notified by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism pursuant to Article 2, subparagraph 6;
3. Other matters concerning policies on Hallyu and Hallyu industries, etc. that the chairperson deems necessary and submits to a meeting of the Council.
(2) The Council shall be composed of one chairperson and no more than 30 members, taking gender into consideration.
(3) The chairperson of the Council shall be the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, and the members of the Council shall be the following persons: <Amended on October 1, 2025; December 30, 2025>
1. The Vice Minister of Finance and Economy, the Vice Minister of Science and ICT, the Vice Minister of Education, the Vice Minister of Foreign Affairs, the Vice Minister of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs, the Vice Minister of Trade and Industry, the Vice Minister of Health and Welfare, the Vice Minister of Oceans and Fisheries, the Vice Minister of SMEs and Startups, the Vice Minister of Planning and Budget, the Vice Chairperson of the Broadcasting, Media and Communications Commission, the Deputy Minister of Food and Drug Safety, and the Deputy Administrator of the Korea Heritage Service. In such cases, for an agency with more than one vice minister, the vice minister designated by the minister of that agency shall serve;
2. Persons appointed by the chairperson from among persons with extensive expertise and experience in Hallyu and Hallyu industries, etc.
(4) The term of office of a member appointed under paragraph (3) 2 shall be two years; provided that, where the Council is dissolved pursuant to paragraph (6), the member's term of office shall expire at the time of dissolution.
(5) The Council shall have one secretary, who shall be a person designated by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism from among public officials belonging to the Senior Civil Service of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(6) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may dissolve the Council where the Minister deems that the purpose for which the Council was established has been achieved.
(7) Matters necessary for the operation of the Council, other than those prescribed in paragraphs (1) through (6), shall be determined by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism.

Article 6 (Fact-Finding Surveys)
(1) Fact-finding surveys under Article 8(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "fact-finding surveys") shall be conducted as regular surveys or ad hoc surveys. Regular surveys shall be conducted annually, and ad hoc surveys shall be conducted where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems an additional survey necessary, such as where there is a rapid change in the market conditions of Hallyu industries, etc.
(2) A fact-finding survey shall include the following matters:
1. Perceptions of Hallyu and Hallyu industries, etc. by country;
2. Market conditions of Hallyu industries, etc.;
3. Other matters for which the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems a fact-finding survey necessary to promote Hallyu industries, etc.
(3) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may commission an institution, corporation, or organization with expertise and personnel for promoting Hallyu industries, etc. to conduct a fact-finding survey.

Article 7 (Annual Reports)
(1) To prepare the report on the results of implementing the master plan and implementation plan and related matters under Article 9(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "annual report"), the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, the heads of local governments, relevant institutions or organizations, and others to submit necessary data.
(2) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall prepare the annual report using the data submitted pursuant to paragraph (1), the results of fact-finding surveys, and other relevant materials.

Article 8 (Training of Specialized Personnel)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, and the heads of local governments may, pursuant to Article 10(1) of the Act, support the following projects for training specialized personnel in related fields to promote Hallyu industries, etc.:
1. Projects for developing programs and teaching materials necessary for training specialized personnel;
2. Projects concerning education, training, research, and other activities necessary for training specialized personnel;
3. Other projects deemed necessary by the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism, the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, and the heads of local governments for training specialized personnel.
(2) The procedures and methods for support under paragraph (1), and other related matters, shall be governed by the Subsidy Management Act and the Act on the Management of Local Government Subsidies.

Article 9 (Establishment and Operation of the Hallyu Industry Information System)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may request the heads of relevant central administrative agencies, heads of local governments, heads of institutions and organizations related to Hallyu industries, etc., and others to provide information necessary to establish and operate the Hallyu industry information system under Article 12(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Hallyu industry information system").
(2) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism shall endeavor to ensure that the information in the Hallyu industry information system remains accurate and up to date.

Article 10 (Promotion of Business Start-ups in Hallyu Industries, Etc.)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may, pursuant to Article 16(1) of the Act, provide necessary support for business start-ups falling under any of the following subparagraphs:
1. Business start-ups for the development and production of products or the development of services related to Hallyu industries, etc.;
2. Business start-ups for the distribution and export of products and services related to Hallyu industries, etc.;
3. Other business start-ups in fields where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems support necessary to promote business start-ups in Hallyu industries, etc., and the growth and development of business founders.
(2) The methods, procedures, and other matters concerning support under paragraph (1) shall be as prescribed in the Subsidy Management Act.

Article 11 (Support for Investment in Hallyu Business Operators)
The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may, pursuant to Article 17(3) of the Act, undertake the following programs to support investment in Hallyu business operators:
1. Programs to identify and develop investors with outstanding investment capabilities;
2. Programs to support exchanges of information among investors on technologies, markets, and other matters relating to Hallyu industries, etc.;
3. Programs for surveys and research to improve the institutional framework for attracting investment;
4. Other programs that the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism deems necessary to promote investment in Hallyu business operators.

Article 12 (Requirements for Designating Specialized Agencies, Etc.)
(1) The Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism may designate an institution, corporation, or organization that meets all of the following requirements as an agency dedicated to promoting the Hallyu industry under Article 18(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as a "specialized agency"):
1. Be an institution, corporation, or organization falling under any of the following items:
(a) A public institution under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions;
(b) An institution, corporation, or organization established under the Civil Act or another Act that the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism recognizes as possessing expertise in international exchanges and overseas expansion by Hallyu business operators;
(c) An institution invested in or funded by a local government under Article 2(1) of the Act on the Operation of Institutions Invested in or Funded by Local Governments;
2. Have a dedicated organizational unit and dedicated personnel necessary to carry out the programs set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 13(1) of the Act.
(2) An institution, corporation, or organization seeking designation as a specialized agency under Article 18(1) of the Act shall submit to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism an application for designation in the form prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister, accompanied by documents demonstrating that it meets all of the requirements set forth in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).
(3) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism designates a specialized agency, the Minister shall issue to the institution, corporation, or organization a certificate of designation as a specialized agency in the form prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister, and shall publicly announce that fact on the website of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(4) The head of a specialized agency shall formulate detailed program plans and plans for the disbursement of funds for carrying out the programs set forth in the subparagraphs of Article 13(1) of the Act, and shall submit them to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism each year.

Article 13 (Procedures for Establishing an Association, etc.)
(1) Where Hallyu business operators intend to establish an association under Article 21(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Association"), at least 50 Hallyu business operators shall act as promoters, prepare articles of incorporation, and, following a resolution of the inaugural general meeting, apply to the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism for authorization.
(2) The articles of incorporation under paragraph (1) shall include the following matters:
1. The purpose and name;
2. The location of the principal office;
3. Matters concerning eligibility for membership, admission and withdrawal, and the rights and obligations of members;
4. Matters concerning the affairs of the Association and their execution;
5. Matters concerning officers;
6. Matters concerning the general meeting;
7. Matters concerning organization and operation;
8. Matters concerning assets and accounting;
9. Matters concerning amendments to the articles of incorporation;
10. Matters concerning dissolution and the disposition of remaining assets.
(3) Where the Minister of Culture, Sports and Tourism authorizes the establishment of the Association pursuant to Article 21(1) of the Act, the Minister shall post a public notice of that fact on the website of the Ministry of Culture, Sports and Tourism.
(4) The Association may carry out the following projects:
1. Research and development projects related to the promotion of Hallyu industries, etc. and the holding of related academic conferences;
2. Holding domestic and international cultural exchange events related to Hallyu;
3. Cooperative projects with domestic and foreign private organizations related to Hallyu;
4. Other projects necessary to promote the sound development of Hallyu industries, etc. and the common interests of Hallyu business operators.
(5) Except as otherwise provided in this Decree, the provisions of the Civil Act concerning incorporated associations shall apply mutatis mutandis to the Association.

