ADDENDA <No. 35461, April 22, 2025>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on April 23, 2025.

Article 2 (Special Cases Concerning Formulation, etc. of Master Plans and Implementation Plans)
(1) Notwithstanding Article 3(1), the first master plan to be formulated after this Decree enters into force shall be formulated by September 30, 2026.
(2) Notwithstanding Article 4(2), the first implementation plan to be formulated after this Decree enters into force shall be formulated by December 31, 2026.

ADDENDA (Presidential Decree on Partial Amendment of 306 Statutes and Regulations to Reflect Government Reorganization) <No. 35811, October 1, 2025>

This Decree shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation: Provided, That, among the Presidential Decrees amended by this Decree, amendments to Presidential Decrees that were promulgated before this Decree enters into force but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective enforcement dates of those Presidential Decrees.

ADDENDA (Decree on the Organization of the Ministry of Finance and Economy) <No. 35947, December 30, 2025>

Article 1 (Enforcement Date)
This Decree shall enter into force on January 2, 2026: Provided, That, among the Presidential Decrees amended pursuant to Article 6 of the Addenda, amendments to Presidential Decrees that were promulgated before this Decree enters into force but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective enforcement dates of those Presidential Decrees.

Articles 2 through 5 Omitted.

Article 6 (Amendment of Other Statutes and Regulations)
(1) through (155) Omitted.

(156) The Enforcement Decree of the Framework Act on the Promotion of the Hallyu Industry shall be partially amended as follows:

In the first sentence of Article 5(3)1, "Vice Minister of Economy and Finance" shall be replaced with "Vice Minister of Finance and Economy", and "Vice Minister of SMEs and Startups" shall be replaced with "Vice Minister of SMEs and Startups, Vice Minister of Planning and Budget".

(157) through (313) Omitted.
